# Push the Limit ({5}{R}{R}): "Return all Mount and Vehicle cards from your graveyard to the battlefield. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step.
# Vehicles you control become artifact creatures until end of turn. Creatures you control gain haste until end of turn."
# Turn 1: Bot1's Faithless Looting discards Smuggler's Copter and Caustic Bronco; Looting itself stays in the graveyard after it resolves. Bot2's own Looting
# (turn 2) discards its Caustic Bronco, which is not Bot1's to return. Bot2 has a Smuggler's Copter on the battlefield, Bot1 another one (turn 3).
# Turn 7: Push the Limit returns Copter and Bronco (not Looting, not Bot2's Bronco); Bot1's other Copter and the returned one become artifact
# creatures, Bot2's Copter does not; the returned Bronco and both Copters have haste (they are creatures when the last sentence resolves)
# and the returned ones are not summoning sick. At the beginning of the end step Bronco and the returned Copter are sacrificed and the other Copter stays.

